+                <select aria-label="Days users can postpone" className="mt-2 w-full rounded-lg border border-overlay/15 bg-bg-elevated p-3 text-text-primary" value={draft.days} onChange={e => { setDraft({ ...draft, days: Number(e.target.value) }); setSaved(false); action.reset(); }}>{Array.from({ length: 14 }, (_, i) => i + 1).map(n => <option key={n} value={n}>{n} {n === 1 ? 'day' : 'days'}</option>)}</select>
+              </label>}
+            </fieldset>
+            <div className="rounded-lg bg-overlay/5 p-4 text-sm text-text-secondary space-y-2"><h3 className="font-medium text-text-primary">What happens on devices</h3>
+              <p>{selected && inherit && data?.shared ? installationPolicySummary(data.shared) : installationPolicySummary(draft)}.</p>
+              <p>Prompts use the app’s installer toolkit. If no user is signed in, or the app does not need to close, installation may run silently. After the choice period, the next Intune attempt installs the update.</p>
+              <p>Reminders follow Intune’s retry checks. This does not schedule an exact installation time, a login, or a reboot.</p>
+            </div>
